<%--
Wysiwyg_Input

WYSIWYG editor widget for forms using Quill. Edits a Rich_Text value.

$placeholder - Placeholder text
$seeder - Seeder function name for test data

Widget interface:
- val() - Get/set a Rich_Text INSTANCE (never a string)
- seed() - Fills with random content

This widget accepts Rich_Text and refuses everything else, so a column whose
$text_types entry is not Rich_Text cannot be wired to it by accident.

There is no sanitize-at-every-layer checklist to follow any more: Rich_Text filters
its own writes, renders itself on a live page through its PRINTER component, and
renders itself into a server-generated document through to_html(). A call site never
chooses an escaping function for this value, which is the whole reason the type exists.

Usage:
<Wysiwyg_Input $name="description" $placeholder="Describe the project..." />
--%>
<Define:Wysiwyg_Input extends="Form_Input_Abstract">
    <div $sid="editor" class="Wysiwyg_Input__editor"></div>
    <input type="hidden" $sid="hidden_input" />
</Define:Wysiwyg_Input>
